1. DEFINITIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Software" means the ClipLink source code, binaries, documentation, and assets
distributed under this License, including any modified versions.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
License.

"Repository" means the canonical ClipLink source repository at
https://github.com/ichigo-k/cliplink.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software, in whole or in part, that
directly or indirectly generates revenue. This includes, without limitation:

  (a) selling, licensing, renting, or leasing the Software or any derivative
      of it;
  (b) bundling or embedding the Software in a product or service that is sold,
      licensed, or offered on a paid or freemium basis;
  (c) offering the Software, or a service built on it, as a hosted or managed
      product;
  (d) using the Software as part of a paid consulting, support, or integration
      offering.

Internal use by a for-profit organisation — employees using ClipLink to move
their own clipboard between their own devices — is NOT Commercial Use.

"Non-Commercial Use" means any use that is not Commercial Use. This includes
personal use, education, academic research, registered non-profit use, and
unpaid hobby or community projects.

"Gross Revenue" means all revenue You receive that is attributable to a
product or service falling under Commercial Use, before costs and deductions.

