------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A PAID LICENCE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Commercial Use is not permitted under Section 2. To make Commercial Use of the
Software, You must obtain a commercial licence, which is granted on either of
the following terms, at Your choice:

  (a) REVENUE SHARE. You pay five percent (5%) of Gross Revenue to the
      ClipLink project, calculated per calendar quarter and paid within
      thirty (30) days of the end of that quarter; or

  (b) NEGOTIATED LICENCE. You agree separate terms in writing with the
      copyright holders — a flat fee, a per-seat fee, or any other arrangement
      both parties accept.

SMALL-SCALE EXEMPTION. If Your total Gross Revenue attributable to the
Software is less than one thousand United States dollars (US$1,000) in any
rolling twelve-month period, no payment is due for that period. You still owe
the obligations in Section 4. This exemption exists so that side projects,
early-stage products, and small experiments are not blocked by paperwork.

To arrange a commercial licence, or to report revenue under (a), open an issue
titled "Commercial licence" at https://github.com/ichigo-k/cliplink/issues, or
contact the maintainers through the Repository.

